    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0835" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">647.116/139: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Melbourne</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dye</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Melbourne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-06-01T18:00:00+10:00">June 1, 1936—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 1—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From Moffat. I presented note to Sir George Pearce this morning. Although he
                    recognized the drawbacks and risks inherent in a deliberate attempt to divert
                    trade, he held out no hope of any modification of the Government’s policy or of
                    nondiscrimination in its application. Details of conversation by
                        despatch.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d596-f1"/> Returning to Sydney, due
                    Wednesday evening. [Moffat.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dye</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
